.TH "GLESHA-CLEANUP" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glesha-cleanup \- remove eligible local archive copies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glesha cleanup SET|\-\-all [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Preview managed import/restore archive files and reclaimable bytes; require [y/N]
before removing them. Keep catalogs, registry, configuration, source data and
explicitly chosen archive outputs. Remote objects are never deleted.
Skip sets with pending operations, unfinished imports/restores, incomplete snapshots
or unpublished catalogs. Check exact remote versions and revalidate local hashes
before removal. Metadata checks do not download payloads or request retrieval.
.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B \-\-progress MODE
auto, plain or off (default auto). JSON mode emits JSON progress on stderr; off disables it.

.TP
.B \-\-format FORMAT
plain or json; status also supports table and csv. JSON results use stdout.

.TP
.B \-\-all
Process all locally registered sets.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Preview without removing files.
.TP
.B \-\-assume-yes
Skip confirmation; retain all safety checks.
.TP
.B \-\-L STRING
debug, info, warn, error or silent (default "info")
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file STRING
separate catalog passphrase file
.TP
.B \-\-color STRING
yes, no or auto; always/never aliases accepted (default "auto")
.TP
.B \-\-config STRING
TOML configuration file
.TP
.B \-\-env STRING
explicit credential environment file
.TP
.B \-\-h
show help
.TP
.B \-\-help
show help
.TP
.B \-\-log\-level STRING
debug, info, warn, error or silent (default "info")
.TP
.B \-\-version
show version; \-version is also accepted.
.TP
.B \-v
Alias for \-\-version.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha cleanup docs \-\-dry-run
glesha cleanup docs \-\-env /secure/cloud.env
glesha cleanup \-\-all \-\-assume-yes \-\-env /secure/cloud.env
.fi
